[{:rule-id "rule-ai", :item {:feed-id "hn-frontpage", :item-id "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49858513", :title "Show HN: Reladraw – A diagram language where you decide where to place things", :link "https://github.com/reladraw/reladraw", :published-at #inst "2026-09-26T17:10:40.000-00:00", :content "I love making diagrams to help understand, plan, etc. However, the options are (A) auto-placement languages like Mermaid or Graphviz (which don't let me decide how the diagram looks), or (B) software like Draw.io which are powerful but are very time consuming (and inefficient for agents to manipulate). I wanted to have the benefits of both, where you can define a diagram in a diagram language, but also retain a high degree of control over what the diagram looks like. I also wanted this to work well for humans and agents. On the Github link, there's a playground where you can try it out without installation. There's also instructions for a simple npm install and for installing a skill you can use with Claude or other agents. Comments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49858513 Points: 67 # Comments: 15"}, :excerpts [{:text "... and for installing a skill you can use with Claude or other agents. Comments URL:...", :matched-terms ["claude"], :source :content}]}]